UID:gp-qc-general-scholarship-application-2026-10-25@qc-polisci-pathways
DTSTAMP:20261021T053157Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: QC scholarships (General Application)
DESCRIPTION:One general application on QC's AcademicWorks portal (https://q
 c-cuny.academicworks.com/) puts you in the running for most of the college
 's donor scholarships\, based on merit\, need\, major or class year. Fall 
 applications pay for the spring term\, and spring applications pay for the
  fall. A few awards add a short supplemental question at the end.\nWhere a
 nd when: QC Foundation scholarships · one application\, every semester\nW
 ho: Matriculated QC students with a QC email\, including second-degree stu
 dents. The office says most awards are open to students without documentat
 ion\nFor political science: Minister Jason Peck (https://qc-cuny.academicw
 orks.com/opportunities/7654) ($500\; preference for political science majo
 rs and minors)\, Sig and Mary Hecht (https://qc-cuny.academicworks.com/opp
 ortunities/7632) (financial need and a 3.0+ GPA in a social science)\, Swi
 mmer (https://qc-cuny.academicworks.com/opportunities/7597) (preference fo
 r students interested in law) and Brownstein/McDermott (https://qc-cuny.ac
 ademicworks.com/opportunities/7565) ($5\,000\; political theory counts\; 3
 0+ credits and a 3.5+ GPA)\nTip: Apply every semester. The office suggests
